{
  "id": "failed-connect-requests-are-printed-via-dumper-http-connect-",
  "title": "Failed CONNECT requests are printed via Dumper.http_connect_error",
  "kind": "callpath",
  "answers": [
    "Why does mitmdump print nothing for failed CONNECT?",
    "How do I make CONNECT failures show in dumper output?",
    "Which hook fires when a CONNECT fails?"
  ],
  "body": "Failed CONNECT flows never fire `response` or `error` hooks, so Dumper stayed silent.\n- Flow: `proxy/layers/http/__init__.py:HttpStream.handle_connect_regular` (eager strategy: `OpenConnection` err -> sets 502 'Cannot connect to ...' response) -> `handle_connect_finish` sets non-2xx response and yields `HttpConnectErrorHook`.\n- Fix: `addons/dumper.py:Dumper.http_connect_error(self, f)` = `if self.match(f): self.echo_flow(f)` (same as `response`/`error`).\n- Successful CONNECTs still not printed (no hook for them in Dumper).\n- Test: `test/mitmproxy/addons/test_dumper.py:test_http_connect_error`; changelog entry goes under 'Unreleased' in CHANGELOG.md.",
  "applies": "regular/upstream mode CONNECT handling; hook name http_connect_error is from HttpConnectErrorHook",
  "tags": [
    "dumper",
    "connect",
    "hooks"
  ],
